{"parentUuid":"789c8982-00fe-4481-a8d0-5f070a24d520","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01AvAQG2k6VWbTznnkcFBwAA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Discovery is **tree-walking, not commit-walking** — we ignore git history entirely.\n\n**Both stores follow the same shape:**\n\n| Layer | Ref | Discovery entry point |\n|---|---|---|\n| v1 | branch `entire/checkpoints/v1` | `GitStore.ListCommitted` (`committed.go:1127`) |\n| v2 | custom ref `refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/main` | `V2GitStore.ListCommitted` (`v2_read.go:68`) |\n\n**The walk** (`parse_tree.go:303`, shared between v1 and v2):\n\n```\nWalkCheckpointShards(repo, tree, fn):\n  for each top-level entry:\n    keep only directories whose name is exactly 2 chars  ← shard bucket\n    for each child:\n      keep only directories                                ← checkpoint folder\n      cpID = bucket_name + child_name                      ← 12 hex chars\n      fn(cpID, child.tree_hash)\n```\n\n**Then for each checkpoint subtree** (`committed.go:1140-1182`):\n\n1. Read `metadata.json` at the checkpoint root → `CheckpointSummary` (gives `CheckpointsCount`, `FilesTouched`, `Sessions`)\n2. Read `<latestSessionIdx>/metadata.json` → `CommittedMetadata` (gives `Agent`, `SessionID`, `CreatedAt`)\n3. Append a `CommittedInfo` to the result; sort by `CreatedAt` desc\n\n**What this means:**\n\n- The tree at HEAD of `entire/checkpoints/v1` is the source of truth. Old commit subjects, rewritten history, anything in trailers — irrelevant for discovery.\n- All metadata (`CreatedAt`, `Agent`, `FilesTouched`, etc.) comes from JSON files in that tree. There's no fallback to git's commit metadata in normal listing.\n- That's why my earlier `--grep` lookup was fragile and the path-based one is better — it asks git the same shape question (`which commit touched this folder`) that the discovery itself implicitly relies on.\n\nSo when you see `(unknown time)` in the dry-run today, it means: the checkpoint folder exists in the v1 tree, but `<latestSession>/metadata.json` either doesn't exist, can't be parsed, or has an empty/zero `created_at`. That's a real data quirk, not a discovery bug."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":776,"cache_read_input_tokens":147464,"output_tokens":1434,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":776,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1434,"cache_read_input_tokens":147464,"cache_creation_input_tokens":776,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":776},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoTn2r6tno4P7fYxJEiL","type":"assistant","uuid":"e73f8dfc-1df2-4cea-b5ac-61b93e0867fb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T15:41:56.350Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments","sessionId":"257a1e25-b5cc-4442-a8c8-ac24b40b3c7f","version":"2.1.129","gitBranch":"soph/investigation"}
